window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-097", "name_zh": "物质", "name_en": "matter", "tagline": "赛斯说物质不是摆在那里等你发现的死原料：它是内在实相在外面显化的样子，每一个看起来结实的物体都是一件从没停过的活动固化成的事件，而把它组织起来的是价值完成——所以你感知到的物质，一直有你自己在里面参与造成。", "explanation": "赛斯讲的物质不是宇宙里那堆先存在、后来才长出意识的原料。他的顺序是反过来的：意念与心理结构在先，物质是它们在外面显出来的样子，所以他一面把物质叫作伪装，一面又说它一点都不假——那是你唯一能实实在在操作的一层。这一页立四件事：一，物体看着坚固，其实是一件一直在被重新创造的活动，你看到的永久性主要来自你的时间结构；二，没有你们所谓的无生物，物质的每一个层次都有自己的意识与合作倾向，把它们组织起来的是价值完成，而不是外面那张设计图；三，你的物质环境和你的身体形象是你自己参与造成的，而且大部分在意识之下发生；四，感知不是拍照，你看到的那份物质里有你贡献的部分。至于原子、分子、电子那一层具体怎么做，同标签下的原子和分子那一页去讲——这一页只回答一个问题：物质是什么。", "definitions": [{"zh": "我告诉过你们，你们的物质特性极接近内在实相，是内在实相在物质层面上的一个物质化。", "en": "Your physical nature is, as I have told you, an approximation and materialization of inner reality on a physical level.", "source": "Session 78"}, {"zh": "再次地，我现在在这里说的是很实际的连结，能量形成物质，物质和能量密不可分，物件会从它们的拥有者和周围的环境，获取它们的特质。", "en": "I am speaking again of quite practical connections here, for as energy forms matter, matter and energy are inseparable and objects obtain their character from their owners, and from the circumstances surrounding them.", "source": "Session 201"}, {"zh": "只有由这个观点，物质的真实本质才能被了解。只有由理解这种思想与欲望的经常转译的本质——并没译为字句，而是成为物体——你才能领会你是真正超越情况、时间与环境的。", "en": "It is only from this viewpoint that the true nature of physical matter can be understood. It is only by comprehending the nature of this constant translation of thoughts and desires — not into words now, but into physical objects — that you can realize your true independence from circumstance, time, and environment.", "source": "Session 523"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "物质不是原料，是内在实相在外面显化的样子", "note": "先从第 78 节那句最直白的定义起步：你们的物质特性极接近内在实相，是内在实相在物质层面上的一个物质化。他没有说灵魂住在一堆死材料里，也没有说物质是灵魂之外另有的东西，他说的是同一件事的两个方向——往里看是意念，往外看就是物质。第 254 节把顺序挑明：物质实相的所有面向，首先存在于非客观实相的架构之内。第 825 节说得更干脆：你们宇宙的根源是非物质的，每一个事件不论多伟大或多渺小都在架构二的环境里诞生，物质宇宙是从那个内在架构升起的，而且现在仍然在这样做。第 903 节用了一个很省的字，说物质宇宙是从必然作为它源头的那个实相搬过来的；同一节还提醒，世界过去是、现在也仍然是，在你们所了解的时间和空间之外的次元里被创造的。创造不是在开端那一秒就结束的事。\n\n反直觉的地方在于这并不是修辞。第 705 节立了一条他说适用于任何尺度的说法：内在的意向永远形成任何外在的改变，意识形成环境，而环境本身也是有意识的。第 776 节只给了短短一行口授：存在着相互关系的通道，连接所有的物质，意识从里面流过。第 928 节收尾：意念的世界处处渗透进物质实相，每一个你所知的具体显现都有一个它永远身处其中的非具体对等者，它由那里来，也会朝那里归去。读这一块时记住一件事——赛斯不把物质当底层，他把物质当结果。新手最容易卡住的也是这里：如果按平常的读法把这几段当成诗意比喻，那后面所有关于疾病、天气、身体的话都会变得没道理。", "src": "早期课第2册第 78 节；早期课第6册第 254 节；《未知的实相卷二》第 705 节；《个人与群体事件的本质》第 825 节；《心灵的本质》第 776 节；《梦、进化与价值完成》第 903、928 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 78 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 254 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 705 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 825 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 776 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 903 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 928 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "顺序是反的：先有内在，后有物质", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e0623", "zh": "条件反射作用于是也必须要活跃起来，直觉会对你们有所帮助。我告诉过你们，你们的物质特性极接近内在实相，是内在实相在物质层面上的一个物质化。所以一些简单的行动，如漫步在雨中、躺在草地上、迎风而行，都是通往心灵体验的途径。", "en": "Conditioning therefore must also be enlivened, and intuition will help you here. Your physical nature is, as I have told you, an approximation and materialization of inner reality on a physical level. Therefore, such simple activities as walking in the rain, lying upon grass, walking in windy weather, all represent gateways to psychic experience.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第78节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "78", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e1683", "zh": "现在。你知道，物质实相的所有面向首先存在非客观实相的架构之内。", "en": "（“Good evening, Seth, Now. As you know, all aspects of physical reality first exist within the framework of nonobjective reality.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第254节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "254", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3640", "zh": "你们宇宙的根源是非物质的，而每一个事件不论多伟大或多渺小，都在“架构二”的环境里诞生。那么，你们的物质宇宙是由那内在架构升起的，并且继续在这样做。", "en": "The origin of your universe is nonphysical, and each event, however grand or minute, has its birth in the Framework 2 environment. Your physical universe arose from that inner framework, then, and continues to do so.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第825节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "825", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3798", "zh": "以一种说法，物质宇宙是从必然为其源头的另一个实相“搬过来的”。世界本是，现在也还是，在时间及你们所了解的空间之外的次元（热切的）创造的。", "en": "In a manner of speaking (underlined), the physical universe is “transposed” upon another reality that must be its source. The world was and is created in dimensions outside of time, and outside of space as you understand it (intently).", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第903节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "903", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3260", "zh": "以你们的说法，“对自己的意识”之发展并不是因为你们的族类在任何外在的环境里获胜之故，事实上，任何一个人的那种“对自己的意识”是依赖着存在于矿物、植物与动物世界之间经常而奇迹性的合作。内在的意向永远形成任何外在的改变，这适用于你们用到的任何尺度。意识形成环境，环境本身是有意识的（有力的）。原子与分子本身在他们自己的可能性范围内运作，以它们自己的方式，它们“渴求”所有可能的发展，当它们形成活生生的生物时，它们变成了物种改变的一个物质基础。身体的可适应性并不只是一种适应的机制或性质，细胞有你们还未发现的内在能力，它们在自己内涵藏着它们曾为其一部分的所有“先前”形成之记忆。", "en": "In your terms, consciousness of self did not develop because of any exterior circumstances in which your species won out, so to speak. In fact, that consciousness of self in any person is dependent upon the constant, miraculous cooperations that exist between the mineral, vegetable, and animal worlds.3 The inner intent always forms any exterior alteration. This applies on any scale you use. Consciousness forms the environment. The environment itself is conscious (forcefully). Atoms and molecules themselves operate in their own fields of probabilities. In their own ways, they “yearn” toward all probable developments. When they form living creatures they become a physical basis for species alteration. The body’s adaptability is not simply an adjusting mechanism or quality. The cells have inner capabilities that you have not discovered. They contain within themselves memory of all the “previous” forms they have been a part of.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第705节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "705", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "这不是比喻", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e3544", "zh": "口授：有相互关系的通道，连接所有的物质——意识流过的通道。", "en": "Dictation. There are channels of interrelatedness, connecting all physical matter — channels through which consciousness flows.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第776节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "776", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3848", "zh": "意念的世界处处渗透进物质实相，但意念，纵使在未被表达时，也拥有自己的组织、呼应，及自己的活动和发展的圈子。那么，主要事件从所有意念于其中发源的意念实相浮出，而透过天然的呼应统合那些意念。每个你所知的具体显现都有它永远对其中的非具体的对等者，它由之而来，并且也会朝之归去。", "en": "(A one-minute pause at 9:34.) Give us a moment…. The world of ideas everywhere permeates physical reality, but ideas, even when they are unexpressed, possess their own organizations, correspondences,3 their own spheres of motion and development. Master events emerge from that reality of idea, now, from which all ideas originate, uniting these through the use of natural correspondences. Every physical manifestation that you know has its nonphysical counterpart, in which it is always couched, from which it came, and to which it will return.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第928节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "928", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "你以为的物体，其实是一件没停过的活动", "note": "第 60 节先把靶子立起来：模式的存在给人一种永久不变的错觉，这是严重的误导；紧跟着他说必须考虑物质被持续不断创造的方式，以及感官在这里扮演的角色。第 514 节指出错觉的来源——你自己的时间结构使你误以为物质有相当的永恒性，而你对里面经常发生的变化视而不见，肉体感官尽可能把你关在一个非常形式化的实相里。第 684 节换了个说法：身体的物质实相只是一个仿佛的常数，处在一个仿佛不变的物质存在里。第 725 节最实用：你的身份一直在改变，却始终保留着永久感，那种永久感骑在无尽的变化上，它事实上依赖那些物质上、灵性上与心灵上的改变；以你们的说法，如果这些改变不经常发生，你的身体就会死。\n\n第 71 节举了一片草：你称它的某一部分为一片叶子，但组成它的物质既不静止也不永久，所以严格说并不是某个物体在成长。第 73 节接着说得更细：物质里的能量即生即灭，能量不断建构、穿上物质的外衣，而物质在某些情况下是能量的同时表现。这一句是理解物体为什么不像它看起来那样结实的关键。第 780 节留了一个对照，帮你摸到两种秩序的分别：物质的实体不能互相穿透，一张桌子不能穿过一把椅子；精神上的事件却可以混合、穿过彼此而仍保住自己的焦点。赛斯这一块想说的不是世界不真实，而是它真实的方式和看起来的不一样——物体是被暂时固定住的事件。", "src": "早期课第2册第 60、71、73 节；《灵魂永生》第 514 节；《未知的实相卷一》第 684 节；《未知的实相卷二》第 725 节；《心灵的本质》第 780 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 60 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 71 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 73 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 514 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 684 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 725 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 780 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "永久不变是一种错觉", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e0353", "zh": "模式的存在给人一种永久不变的错觉，这是严重的误导。这里有太多要说的东西，因为有必要考虑物质持续不断被创造的方式，以及感官所扮演的角色。", "en": "The existence of the patterns gives the illusion of a permanence of matter that is highly misleading. There is so much to be said here, as it is also necessary to consider the ways in which physical material is constantly created, and to consider the role of the senses.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第60节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "60", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2585", "zh": "因此我们的环境是由精致的不平衡所构成，而容许“改变”尽情的活动。你自己的时间结构使你误以为物质有相当的永恒性，而你对其中经常的变化视而不见。你的肉体感官尽可能地限制你只感知一个非常形式化的实相。通常，只有经由直觉的应用，以及在睡梦中，你才能知觉，你自己的或任何别的意识本质上是在快乐地变化的。", "en": "Our environment therefore is composed of exquisite imbalances, where change is allowed full play. Your own time structure misleads you into your ideas of the relative permanency of physical matter, and you close your eyes to the constant alterations within it. Your physical senses confine you as best they can to the perception of a highly formalized reality. Only through the use of the intuitions and in sleep and dream states, as a rule, can you perceive the joyfully changing nature of your own, and any, consciousness.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第514节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "514", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3194", "zh": "那么，在身体内伟大的沟通系统是依靠这些单位经常不断的内在涨落与流动。在一个层面上，身体存活之本身大半取决于这些单位对选择性与重要意义的癖好。然而，身体的物质实相也是在一个仿佛不变的物质存在里的一个仿佛的常数。", "en": "The great communication system within the body itself is dependent, then, upon the constant inner flux and flow of these units. On one level the body’s very survival is largely determined by the units’ propensities for selectivity and significance. Also, however, the body’s physical reality is a seeming constant in a seemingly constant physical existence.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第684节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "684", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3371", "zh": "以多少同样的方式，你的身份经常的改变，纵使你维持着你的永久感。那种永久感骑在无尽的变化上——它事实上依赖那些物质上、灵性上与心灵上的改变。举例来说，以你们的说法，如果它们不经常发生的话，你的身体会死。再次的，细胞并不只是凑巧组成你们器官的微小而看不见的粒子。它们也拥有它们自己的意识，而那种的意识统合了所有的具体物质。", "en": "(Long pause, eyes closed. Jane’s delivery had slowed considerably.) In somewhat the same way your identity changes constantly, even while you retain your sense of permanence. That sense of permanence rides upon endless changes — it is actually dependent upon those physical, spiritual, and psychic changes. In your terms, for example, if they did not occur constantly your body would die. The cells, again, are not simply minute, handy, unseen particles that happen to compose your organs. They also possess consciousnesses of their own. That [kind of] consciousness unites all physical matter.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第725节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "725", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "一片叶子和一张桌子", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e0533", "zh": "意识在物质场域中的形式是由它自己的强度与能力决定。意识硬挤进物质里面。那么，你们应该明白，虽然你们称草的某个部分为草的一片叶子，但组成它的物质不是静止不动或永久不变的，并不是某个物体在成长，因为组成它的物质既非静止的，也不是永久的。", "en": "The form that consciousness takes in the field of matter is determined by its own strength and capacity. Consciousness forces its way into matter. You should see, then, that though you call a particular portion of grass one blade of grass, the matter that composes it is not static or permanent, and it is not a particular physical object growing, since the matter that composes it is neither static or permanent.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第71节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "71", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e0563", "zh": "原子与分子，在物质里的能量，即生即灭。能量不断持续建构，穿上物质的伪装外衣，但物质在某些情况下，是能量的同时表现。", "en": "The atoms and molecules, energy in matter, appear and disappear instantaneously. Energy constantly is constructed into the guise of matter, but matter is the simultaneous expression of energy under certain conditions.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第73节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "73", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3549", "zh": "以形而上的术语来说，你多少以相同的方式在你心灵或灵魂里存在。身份显然主要是心灵上而非物质上的环境。物质的实体不能相互穿透，就如一张桌子不能穿透一把椅子。精神上的事件却不同。他们相互参杂混合，而且彼此穿透，而仍能维持它自己的焦点。它们能以事件在实质层面交感的同样方式，在心灵层面交感，但却没有实质的限制。那么，你虽然是你心灵的一部分，你的身份感仍然是不可侵犯的。它不会在一个更大的自己中沉没或消减，它带着它自己完整性的印记——一个神圣的记号。它跟随它自己的焦点，自知其为自己，纵使当它作为自己的存在可能，只是另一个「身份」的一部分。", "en": "In metaphysical terms, you have your being in your psyche or soul in somewhat the same manner. Identities are obviously psychic environments, primarily, rather than physical ones. Physical objects cannot move through each other, as a table cannot move through a chair. Mental events behave differently. They can mix and merge, move through each other while still maintaining their own focus. They can interact on psychic levels in the way that events do on physical levels, but without physical restrictions. Though you are a portion of your psyche, then, your identity is still inviolate. It will not be submerged or annihilated in a greater self. It carries a stamp — a divine mark — of its own integrity. It follows its own focus, and knows itself as itself, even while its own existence as itself may be but a portion of another “identity.”", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第780节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "780", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "没有死的物质，只有你还没认出它有意识", "note": "第 62 节先把底线摆出来：不用说也知道，在所有物质背后、也在某种程度上在所有物质之内，都有一种意识、一种意识能量。第 796 节把常识里那个无生物的概念直接撤掉——用你们的说法并没有无生物，只有某一个点你认出它有被你归给生命的那些特性，也就是说，界线是你自己按武断的要求划的。第 2 节讲《健康之道》开头那段说得更广：每种生物生来都为自己骄傲、爱自己，而同样的自我认可不只被你以为的生物经验到，也被原子、分子及所有阶层的物质经验着。\n\n新手会在这里问：一粒石头也有意识？第 267 节的回答讲的是组织而不是聪明：他说我给过你们物质本质的资料，它应该说清每个分子都有它自己浓缩、编码过的意识，如果涉入其中的意识既不合作也不理解，任何一种完形或形式都不会出现。第 66 节把这层意思再说一遍并留了一个关键缺口：原子与分子在自己之内缺乏强大的组织天分，是那个个体的能量在帮助这个模式成形。所以赛斯说的不是每粒东西都像一个小人，而是物质从来不是被动的原料，它有它自己的理解与合作倾向。第 582 节只把话带到边界——他说你的更大实相由你感知不到的、在物质的强度范围之上或之下的原子与分子组成，而它们都以自己的方式拥有意识。再细的那一层，同标签下的原子和分子那一页去讲。", "src": "早期课第2册第 62、66 节；早期课第6册第 267 节；《灵魂永生》第 582 节；《心灵的本质》第 796 节；《健康之道》第 2 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 62 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 66 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 267 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 582 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 796 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 2 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "物质之内有意识", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e0383", "zh": "到这个时候，你们应该知道我们谈物质的资料有多优秀了。我先前说过，这种资料很少发生扭曲。这还有很多要谈。不用说，在所有物质背后，以及某种程度在所有物质之内，都有一种意识，意识能量。", "en": "By this time you should know that our material on material is excellent. I mentioned earlier that very little distortion occurs in such material. There is very much to be covered. It goes without saying then, that there is consciousness of a kind, conscious energy, behind and to some extent within all material.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第62节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "62", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3579", "zh": "并没有你们所谓的无生物。仅只有一个点，你们认知它有你们归属为生命或生存状态的特性——符合你们武断地订下的要求的那一点。", "en": "There is no such thing, in your terms, as nonliving matter. There is simply a point that you recognize as having the characteristics that you have ascribed to life, or living conditions — a point that meets the requirements that you have arbitrarily set.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第796节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "796", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3920", "zh": "每种生物生来都为自己骄傲，并且爱它自己。那同样的自我认可也以种种不同的方式，不但被如你们以为的生物，也被原子、分子及所有阶层的物质所经验。", "en": "Each creature is born proud of itself, and loving itself. That same self-approval is also experienced in varying ways not only by creatures as you think of them, but also by atoms and molecules, and by all orders of matter.", "source": "健康之道 · 第2节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "2", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "意识不合作，就没有形式", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e1763", "zh": "我给你的物质本质相关资料应该清楚表明，每个分子都有它自己浓缩、编码过的意识，要是涉入其中的意识既不合作也不理解，就不会出现任何一种完形或形式。", "en": "The material that I have given you on the nature of matter should make it clear that every atom and molecule has its own condensed, coded consciousness, and that no gestalt or formation of any kind can occur without the cooperation and comprehension of the consciousnesses involved.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第267节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "267", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e0443", "zh": "我说过，每一个物质建构都是由原子和分子组成，每个原子和分子都含有浓缩理解与整体意识。在它们自己之内，缺乏强大的组织天分，并且这个模式的建构受惠于个体的能量。", "en": "I have mentioned that each physical construction is composed of atoms and molecules, which also possess a generalized consciousness and capsule comprehension. They lack strong organizational tendencies in themselves, and it is the individual’s energy which aids in this formation.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第66节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "66", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2868", "zh": "那么我们在谈的是多次元的实相。全我或存有或灵魂永不能以三次元的形式完全地具体化，但它的一部分却能被投射入那个次元，在时间上伸展到这么多年，占据了这么多空间等等。这存有把这整个事件，这整个的人——事与其时间因素，或你们所谓的“年纪”只看作是另一个特性或次元。不过，这“人——事”并没被切断，只是它的更大的实相不能在三次元内展现而已。反之，它是由你感知不到的、在物质的强度范围之上或之下的原子与分子所组成——而所有这些以它们自己的方式都拥有意识。", "en": "We are speaking then of multidimensional reality. The whole self or entity or soul can never be completely materialized in three-dimensional form. A part of it can be projected into that dimension however, extending so many years in time, taking up so much space, and so forth. The entity sees the whole event, the whole person-event, with the time element, or age in your terms, as simply another characteristic or dimension. The person-event is not cut off, however. Its greater reality simply cannot appear within three dimensions. It is instead composed of atoms and molecules that you do not perceive, both above and below the physical range of intensities — and all of these in their own way possess consciousness.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第582节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "582", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "组织物质的不是外部设计图，是价值完成", "note": "第 57 节给了这一块的枢纽：如果你终于明白每一个物质粒子都包含它自己的内在初始意识，那么我们就兜兜转转回到了原地——个体或自己非常重要，它遵循价值完成的法则不断运作，形成尽可能复杂的完形，而在这么做的时候既不侵犯、也不拒绝或否定其他个别的意识；它没有限制，因为它的价值完成有无限的可能性，它能形成的完形有无限的数量。这一段把物质世界的秩序从有没有人设计这个问题里挪开：让物质长成更复杂的东西的，是每一个单位自己要更完整地实现自己。第 149 节把这条落到有机体上：为了价值完成能在物质有机体内显现，某一部分物质成长必须按你们那一连串物质片刻显出来，而发展不是一条线上一个接一个的行动，是透过行动的视角达成的价值完成。\n\n后面几段把这个原理推到宇宙尺度。第 787 节说纯能量的最小单位在你们而言没有重量、在其内不含质量，可它在本性里保存着创造所有各种形式的物质的倾向，以及创造所有可能的宇宙的原动力。第 797 节接着说你们的宇宙不是在某个点、由某一个起始细胞冒出来的，它在各处同时开始存在——当不可见的宇宙的内在脉动达到某种强度，整个物质系统就被自发地孕育了。第 884 节强调物质生命的第一个基础大半是主观的。第 893 节给了一段很有画面感的来历：意识单位同时扮演力量、也扮演势力强大的心理存有，把你们世界的种子种在一个有想象力量的次元里，而那次元生出了物质的实相。第 872 节挡住一个误读：你以为自己是在跟物质的单线发展打交道，其实你面对的是不可想象的创造性——你们物质世界的所有版本都存在，每一个都颇为确信它自己的具体本质。", "src": "早期课第2册第 57 节；早期课第4册第 149 节；《心灵的本质》第 787、797 节；《个人与群体事件的本质》第 872 节；《梦、进化与价值完成》第 884、893 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 57 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 149 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 787 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 797 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 872 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 884 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 893 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "价值完成是组织的原理", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e0323", "zh": "如果你们终于明白每一个物质粒子都包含它自己的内在初始意识，那么，你们就会看到我们兜兜转转回到了原地。个体或自己非常重要。它遵循价值完成的法则不断运作，形成尽可能复杂的完形，但在这么做的时候，它既不侵犯，也不拒绝、否定其他个别的意识。它是没有限制的，因为它的价值完成有无限的可能性，或它能够形成的完形有无限的数量。", "en": "If you then realize that every physical particle contains its own inner and initial consciousness, then you will see that we have come full circle. The individual or the self is all important. It operates to form as complicated a gestalt as possible, following the law of value fulfillment, and yet in so doing it does not either invade, deny or negate other individual consciousness. It is limitless because there are no limits to the possibilities of its value fulfillment, or to the number of gestalts which it can form.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第57节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "57", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e1126", "zh": "因此，就一连串的物理片刻而言，为了价值完成，某一部分物质成长必须在物质有机体之内显现才行。在梦领域以及很多其他系统之内，这一连串的片刻是未知的。发展并不是来自沿着单一方向，一个接一个直线式产生的一连串行动。相反地，发展主要就是价值完成这码事，透过行动的视角而达成，透过在任何行动之内的旅行、顺随它，跟着它改变而达成。讲得更清楚一点好了，我说过行动存在于无限的视角之内，你们所熟悉的多半是在物质系统内，沿着单一连续路线的物质化行动。然后你们体验行动，好像你们正沿着单一线条移动似的，这条线上的每个点代表你们时间中的一个片刻。但是在你们的线条上，代表着任何片刻的一个想像的点上，行动朝着四面八方往外移动。从那个片刻点的立场看来，你们可以想像行动形成一个想像的圆，而那个片刻点就是切点（apex）。但是，这发生在每一个片刻点上。", "en": "A certain portion of physical growth, in terms of a series of physical moments, is therefore necessary for value fulfillment to show itself within a physical organism. Within the dream field and within many other systems, this series of moments is unknown. Development comes not from a series of actions strung out along a single line, one before the other in lengthwise fashion. Instead development is largely a matter of value fulfillment, which is achieved through the perspectives of action, through traveling within any given action, and following it and changing with it. To make this clearer, I have said that action exists within limitless perspectives, and that you are mainly familiar with it as it is materialized along a single line of continuity within the physical system. You experience action then as if you were moving along a single line, each dot on the line representing a moment of your time. But at the imaginary point on your line that represents any given moment, action moves out in all directions. From the standpoint of that moment point, you could imagine action forming an imaginary circle with that point as an apex. But this happens at the point of every moment.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "把这条推到宇宙的开头", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e3559", "zh": "因此，纯能量的最小单位，在你们而言没有重量，在其内包含质量，在其本质内会保持创造所有各种形式的物质之倾向，及创造所有可能的宇宙之原动力。以那种说法，我们无法思考能量，除非把与神或「一切万有」（All That Is）的本质有关的问题带到最前线，因为这些术语是同义的。", "en": "The smallest unit of pure energy, therefore, weighing nothing in your terms, containing within itself no mass, would hold within its own nature the propensity for the creation of matter in all of its forms, the impetus to create all possible universes. In those terms, energy cannot be considered without bringing to the forefront questions concerning the nature of God or All That Is, for the terms are synonymous.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第787节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "787", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3584", "zh": "等一会儿…… 你们的宇宙并非在某一点，也不是由任何一个起始的细胞露出来——却是当不可见的宇宙的内在脉动（inner pulsation）达到了某种强度，而自发地“孕育”了整个的物质系统时，你们的宇宙同时在各处开始存在。", "en": "Your universe did not emerge at any one point, therefore, or with any one initial cell — but everywhere it began to exist at once, as the inner pulsations of the invisible universe reached certain intensities that “impregnated” the entire physical system simultaneously.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第797节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "797", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3738", "zh": "我要强调，我在此所说的不是关于一种灵性的进化，而是一种扩张。然而，我们暂且将讨论限制在世界开始时的意识，强调物质生命的第一个基础大半是主观的，而做梦的情况不只有助于形成你们人类的意识，而且，以那种说法，也用来给人对他的物质环境提供一个稳定的情报来源，并且在所有各物种间用为一个内在的通讯网。", "en": "I want to stress that I am speaking here not so much about a kind of spiritual evolution as I am about an expansion.3 We will for now, however, confine ourselves to a discussion of consciousness in the beginning of the world, stressing that the first basis of physical life was largely subjective, and that the state of dreaming not only helped shape the consciousness of your species, but also in those terms served to provide a steady source of information to man about his physical environment, and served as an inner web of communication among all species. End of dictation.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第884节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "884", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3778", "zh": "从古到今，所有可能被确实化的存有一直是存在的，它们（以前）一直存在，而它们将会一直存在。因其特性，一切万有必须以它所有可能的形式存在（be all that it ever be），因此，存在不可能有终结——而以那种说法，也没有开始。但以你们的世界而言，意识单位同时扮演为力量，以及扮演为势力强大的心理存有，把你们世界的种子种在一个有想象力量的次元里，而这次元生出了物质的实相。以你们的说法，那些存有是你们的祖先——但（它们）并非只是你们的，却是所有形成你们世界的意识的祖先。", "en": "All possible entities that can ever be actualized always exist. They [have] always existed and they always will exist. All That Is must, by its characteristics, be all that it can ever be, and so there can be no end to existence—and, in those terms, no beginning. But in terms of your world the units of consciousness, acting both as forces and as psychological entities of massive power, planted the seeds of your world in a dimension of imaginative power that gave birth to physical form. In your terms those entities are your ancestors—and yet [they are] not yours alone, but the ancestors of all the consciousnesses that make up your world.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第893节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "893", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3710", "zh": "我了解，看起来好像有些物种已消失了，但再次的，你必须记得可能性，而那些族类只不过曾随着可能地球之模式“发展”，你并不只是与物质的单线发展打交道，却是在与一个不可想象的创造性打交道，在其中，你们物质世界的所有版本都存在着，每一个都颇为确信它自己的具体本质。有一些相当无法言说的分支，虽然在某种出神状态或在经过训练的做梦之帮助下，你也许能瞥见那联系你们公认的地球与其他可能的地球之内在复杂性及沟通网络。你一而再的选择你在物质实相内的时间及焦点，而你的心智保有对与人类有关的许多看似神秘的发展之内在理解。", "en": "(Pause at 10:07.) I understand that it appears that species have vanished, but again you must remember probabilities, and that those species simply “developed” along the patterns of probable earths. You are not just dealing with a one-line development of matter, but of an unimaginable creativity, in which all versions of your physical world exist, each one quite convinced of its physical nature. There are ramifications quite unspeakable, although in certain states of trance, or with the aid of educated dreaming, you might be able to glimpse the inner complications, the webworks of communications that connect your official earth with other probable ones. You choose your time and focus in physical reality again and again, and the mind holds an inner comprehension of many seemingly mysterious developments involving the species.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第872节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "872", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "伪装：你的感官只放行协议好的那一层", "note": "赛斯给物质世界起过一个很不客气的名字。第 37 节说，你们的外在自我被建构起来是为了让你们能应对伪装世界，这也是必要的，但它不可避免地缩窄了你们的关注范围和理解程度；在你的存在期间，你被它聚焦、黏住、安放、集中在你们的物质宇宙上，它处理的是你对伪装物质的操纵。第 94 节把智识也算进来：研究内在实相并不是智识的目的，智识以前和现在都是内我和它自己建构的伪装物质宇宙相联系的一个方法。第 426 节说这套伪装做得有多漂亮：伪装由内我极其巧妙地制造并执行，以致你们必然要把注意力聚焦在已经被创造出来的物质实相里——迷幻药之所以能给人一点对其他实相的窥见，是因为它改了神经内部的运作。第 43 节顺手给了出口：内在感官被赋予最大的自由去脱离伪装。\n\n剩下几段说明伪装不是随便一块幕布，而是有结构的。第 40 节：你们的物质建构只存在于你们自己的层面上，其他本质完全不同的建构与你们的同时存在，而你在太空船里永远找不到它们。第 537 节说得更贴近生活：那些环境就在你所知道的物质世界之中而不为你们知觉，只是你们的感知机制不允许你调到它们的频率范围，你对一个极为特定但有限的场域反应。第 506 节给了强度的说法：能量单位可以退落到低于物质的强度里，也可以穿行于物质之中，穿行时显现为物质。第 287 节把这条推到尽头：当你旅行到某个强度之外，连伪物体都必须消失；再往前是一个没有任何伪装存在的强度范围，然后你会遇到下一个系统的假伪装。第 188 节留了一个有用的中间地带——梦影像基本上比实体物质更具可塑性，却由许多相同的属性组成，因为梦的本质与物质实相的东西之间必定有这种连结。第 49 节顺便解释了为什么睡眠不那么像浪费时间：在睡眠状态中，你们不是用自己的能量把意念转化成耐久的物质伪装模式。", "src": "早期课第1册第 37、40 节；早期课第2册第 43、49 节；早期课第3册第 94 节；早期课第4册第 188 节；早期课第7册第 287 节；早期课第9册第 426、506 节；《灵魂永生》第 537 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 37 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 40 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 43 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 49 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 94 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 188 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 287 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 426 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 506 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 537 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "伪装世界与它的操纵者", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e0178", "zh": "你们的外在自我，被建构来让你们可以应对伪装世界。这是必要的。可是它也不可避免地，缩窄了你们的关注范围和理解程度。在你们的存在期间，外在自我让你们聚焦、长在、放在、专注你们的物质宇宙上。它处理你们对伪装物质的操纵。", "en": "Your outside egos are constructed to enable you to deal with the camouflage world. It is necessary. It necessarily also narrows your concentration and your understanding. During your existence you are focused, you are stuck to, you are placed and centered in, your physical universe by the outside ego. It manages your manipulation of camouflage material.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第37节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "37", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e0736", "zh": "研究或学习内在实相并不是智力的目的。再说一次，智识以前和现在都是内我和它自己建构的伪装物质宇宙联系的一个方法。", "en": "A study or investigation of inner reality was not the purpose of the intellect. The intellect, again, was also and is a means by which the inner self relates itself to the camouflage physical universe which it has itself constructed.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第94节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "94", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2279", "zh": "你们对空间与时间的观念，的确是由你们的神经结构决定的。伪装当然是由内我极其巧妙地制造并执行的，以致你们必然要把注意力聚焦在已被创造出来的物质实相里。迷幻药会改变神经内部的运作，因此能让人对其他实相有一些轻微的窥见。", "en": "Now. Your idea of space and time then is definitely determined by your neurological structure. The camouflage is so craftily executed and created, of course, by the inner self, that you must of necessity focus your attention in the physical reality which has been created. The psychedelic drugs alter the neurological inner workings, and therefore can give some slight glimpses into other realities.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第426节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "426", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e0204", "zh": "你们科学家的宇宙扩展概念，是如此依赖你们自己有限的理论，以至于变得很难把这件事说个明白。我再次恳求你们练习运用心理时间，因为内在感官被赋予了最大的自由去脱离伪装。而且体验因此而来的内在扩展，你们或许就会稍微比较接近和我们真正的宇宙扩展有关的观念。", "en": "Your scientists’ idea of an expanding universe is so dependent upon your own limited theories that it becomes very difficult to make the matter plain. Again I entreat you to practice with the use of psychological time, for here the inner senses are given the greatest freedom from camouflage. And experiencing the resulting inner expansion, you will perhaps come somewhat closer to the ideas involved in our real expanding universe.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第43节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "43", "only_en": true}]}, {"label": "同一个地方叠着别的实相", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e0191", "zh": "飞碟的居民不属于你们自己的层面。我已经提过它们涉及外形两难的问题。在任何这些方面的讨论中，你们必须记住，你们的物质建构只能在你们的层面存在而已。其他的物质建构与你们自己的物质建构同时存在，而且具有完全不一样的本质，它们存在的层面或许你们会称之为水平层面。但你们永远也无法在太空船中看到它们。", "en": "The inhabitants of the flying saucers are not of your own plane. I have mentioned the struggle of form involved. You will have to remember in any of the discussions along these lines that your physical constructions simply do not exist except on your own plane. Other constructions exist simultaneously with your own, of an entirely different nature, also however on what you may call a horizontal plane. But you will never find them in a spaceship.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第40节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "40", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2694", "zh": "这是你们自己对实相本质误解的结果。因此没有一个地方，没有一个特定的地点。这些环境存在于你所知道的物质世界之中而不为你们知觉。其实只是你们的感知机制不允许你调准到它们频率的范围而已。你只对一个极为特定而有限的范围反应。如我以前说过的，其他的实相与你自己的实相共存。在死时你只是舍弃了你自己的物质行头，对不同的范围对准频率，并且对另一套设定反应而已。", "en": "It is the result of your own misinterpretations of the nature of reality. There is no one place therefore, no specific location. These environments exist unperceived by you amid the physical world that you know. Your perceptive mechanisms simply do not allow you to tune in to their ranges. You react to a highly specific but limited field. As I mentioned earlier, other realities coexist with your own at death, for example. You simply divest yourself of physical paraphernalia, tune into different fields, and react to other sets of assumptions.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第537节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "537", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2545", "zh": "能量单位，如我所说，是相对毁不坏的。然而它们可以失去或增益力量，可以退落到低于物质的强度里，也可以穿行于物质之中——穿行时显现为物质——投射过你们的系统。它们活动的那一部分，我们将另行处理。不过那样的情形下，它们显然正处在一个过渡的点上，处在一种“正在生成”的状态。现在，你们愿意的话，可以休息，也可以结束这一节课。", "en": "The energy units, as I told you, are relatively indestructible. They can however lose or gain power, fall back into intensities beneath matter, or go through matter, appearing as matter as they do so, and projecting through your system. We will deal with that portion of their activity separately. In such cases however they are in a point of transition obviously, and in a state of becoming. Now you may take a break or end the session as you prefer.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第506节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "506", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e1876", "zh": "可以说，当你旅行到某个强度之外的时候，甚至连伪物体都必须消失。它们成群存在你自己的系统四周，并与之连结。甚至是缺少伪物体都意味着你已经越过你的伪装系统。如果你可以做到的话，那么你会穿越一个没有任何伪装存在的强度范围，然后你看，你就会遇见下一个系统的假伪装（pseudocamouflage）。根据这个系统，这会是或不会是实质物体。", "en": "When you travel, so to speak, beyond a certain range of intensities, even pseudoobjects must vanish. They exist in a cluster about, and connected to, your own system. The lack of even pseudoobjects obviously means that you have gone beyond your camouflage system. If it were possible for you, you would then travel through a range of intensities in which no camouflage existed. Then you would encounter the pseudocamouflage, you see, of the next system. This would or would not be physical matter, according to the system.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第287节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "287", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e1338", "zh": "梦影像，非灵体投射，在动作时受到某些电子上的限制，这些限制形成了梦宇宙的界限。然而，梦影像几乎都是类似纤维状的投射，是一种近乎稀稀疏疏的组合结构，基本上来说，它们比实体物质还具有可塑性，不过是由许多相同的属性所组成。再说一次，梦的本质与物质实相的东西，两者间必定有这种连结。", "en": "Dream images, not astral projections, operate within certain electrical limits, limits that form the boundaries of the dream universe. Dream images are nevertheless almost fibrous projections, almost a thinned-out composition, more plastic basically than physical matter, but composed of a number of the same properties. For again there must be this connection between the nature of dreams and the matter of physical reality.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第188节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "188", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e0233", "zh": "我已经谈过上这些课背后的原因，并且它们可以被阅读。我们这里有一个微妙的平衡，它本身又包含能量的成长与释放。我先前说过，在梦经验里，就感官而言，你可能会造访一个特定的地点，经验某种程度的时间存续；然而该地点并不在你们的空间里存在并被找到，虽然你在梦里经历了，比如说，5个小时，但它可能只占用钟表时间的一瞬间，而且在心理的梦经验中，肉体也没有和涉及的心理实相成正比而变老。你不受空间束缚，而且很大程度不受时间限制，在睡眠状态中，因为你们不是用你们的能量，把意念转化成耐久的物质伪装模式。", "en": "I have gone into the reasons behind these sessions, and they can be read. We have a delicate balance here, and in the delicate balance itself lies the outgrowth and release of energy. I have mentioned earlier that in a dream experience, as far as the senses are concerned you may visit a particular location, experience a certain time duration; and yet the location does not exist and cannot be found in your space, and though you experience, say, five hours time in your dream, this perhaps takes up merely a flash of clock time, and the physical body does not age during the psychological dream experience in any proportion to the actual psychological reality involved. You are free of space, and to a large degree of time, in the sleeping state, because you are not using your energies to transform ideas into durable physical camouflage patterns.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第49节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "49", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "你创造你自己的物质环境，大部分时候你并不知道", "note": "这一块由第 26 节定调。赛斯说他说的不是你创造一切万有，那只是说你在用同样的方式创造你的物质宇宙，像你呼气在玻璃上留下一片水汽图案一样自动、一样不自觉地。第 240 节把这个说法整理成一份具体清单：每一个个体都会创造实体物质、包括物体在内，也建构自己的肉体形象；连贯性、永久不变的幻相、在空间的位置、颜色与重量，这些全部是以他已经解释过的方式协议达成的。第 68 节举了一个坐在椅子上的人：你和他都感知到马克，可你们谁也没看见马克的马克——他持续不断地用自己的心灵能量、用特定的原子和分子在物质上创造自己的形象。第 302 节把这层外推：物质环境在很多方面可以直接看成肉身自己的延伸，其他意象的物质形态向外辐射，和肉体形象一样处在持续变化中，而这一切全都反映着内在的基本行动。\n\n第 300 节是写给怀疑者的：你仍然必须和物质实相打交道，因为它绝对是内在资料的重现；预期不只在所有感官资料背后，它形成了感官资料；你的物质状况在每一方面都反映着你内在的预期、成就与失败。第 334 节给出唯一的改法——那物质形象或世界里的任何一部分要改变，改变必须先从内我的氛围做起。第 573 节把它从个人放大到集体：在你们的系统里你们直接参与物质实相的形成，你们眼前的自然现像是个人、群众与集体的思想、感觉与情感的具体化。第 162 节留了最刺人的一段，并特别说明这不是什么神秘魔法、也不是装神弄鬼——你是什么取决于你对自己抱持的想法，每个思想都反映在人类组织的实体物质上，因此这个意象的健康状况本来就是你自己的责任。第 340 与第 342 节说清机制的两侧：你想像出来的困境会自己带来让它在物质世界成为实相的条件，而强度带来相应的物质具体化，感官再感知到它，整个循环就闭合了。", "src": "早期课第1册第 26 节；早期课第2册第 68 节；早期课第4册第 162 节；早期课第6册第 240 节；早期课第7册第 300、302 节；早期课第8册第 334、340、342 节；《灵魂永生》第 573 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 26 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 68 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 162 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 240 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 300 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 302 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 334 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 340 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 342 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 573 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "像呼吸在玻璃上留下水汽", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e0127", "zh": "因为我说你用同样的方式创建你的物质宇宙，就像你用你的呼吸在一块玻璃上创造一个蒸汽图案一样，是自动的、无意识的，但这并不表示，你创造了一切万有。它只表示你创造你自己的物质环境。如果我得到你的允许，约瑟，我们明天晚上会面时再谈别的事。", "en": "Because I say that you create your physical universe in the same manner and as automatically and as un-self-consciously as you create with your breath a pattern of steam upon a glass plane, this does not mean that you create All That Is. It merely means that you create your own physical environment. And if I have your permission, Joseph, we will meet tomorrow evening to go into other matters.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第26节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "26", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e1604", "zh": "我告诉过你，每一个个体都会创造实体物质，包括物体在内，也说过他会建构自己的肉体形象。连贯性、永久不变的幻相、在空间的位置、颜色与质量，这些全部都以我已经清楚解释过的方式达成协议。（在第二册，见1964年夏天给出的第60至73节，以及其他很多节。）", "en": "I have told you that each individual creates physical matter, including objects, that he constructs his own physical image. Coherence, the illusion of permanency, placement in space, color and mass, all these are arrived at and agreed upon, in ways that I have clearly explained. （In Volume 2, see the 60th to 73rdsessions, given during the summer of1964, plus many others.）", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第240节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "240", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e0473", "zh": "你和鲁柏感知马克，但你们谁也没有看见马克的马克。他坐在他的椅子上，持续不断在物质上创造他自己的形象，用他自己的心灵能量，用特定的原子和分子来建构他的身体。", "en": "You and Ruburt perceive Mark, and yet neither of you sees Mark’s Mark. As he sits in his chair, constantly he creates his own image physically, using his own psychic energy, and using particular atoms and molecules for the construction of his body.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第68节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "68", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e1918", "zh": "物质环境在很多方面都可以被看成是肉身自己的直接延伸。其他意象的物质形态，你看，向外辐射；这些可能会持续变化，就像肉体形象那样，而这一切全都反映了内在的基本行动。", "en": "The physical environment can be seen in many ways as direct extensions from the physical self. Physical formations of other images, you see, radiating outward; these subject to continual change, as is the physical image, and all of this reflecting the inner and basic action.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第302节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "302", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "你的状况反映你的内在预期", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e1910", "zh": "你仍然必须和物质实相打交道，因为它绝对是内在资料的重现。我不停地说这件事：预期不但在所有的感官资料背后，而且形成了感官资料。我跟你说过——顺便说一下，我可爱的怀疑论者，以前我告诉过你——你创造你自己的物质环境和宇宙。你的物质状况在每一方面都反映着你内在的预期、成就以及失败，而且我也告诉过你，任何疾病都是一个内在扭曲造成的结果。", "en": "You must still deal with physical reality, for it is definitely the representation of inner data. I have said this constantly: Expectation is behind all Sense data, and forms it. I have told you—and incidentally my lovely skeptics I have told you in the past—that you create your own physical environment and universe. Your physical condition in every way is a reflection of your inner expectations, accomplishments, and failures, and I have told you that any illness is the result of an inner distortion.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第300节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "300", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e1996", "zh": "同样的道理，你创造了你的物质形象和世界。如果这个物质形象或世界里的任何部分需要改变的话，那么必须先从内我的氛围改变起。", "en": "In the same manner, you create your physical image and your world. If anything in that physical image or world needs changing, the change must first be made in the atmosphere of the inner self.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第334节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "334", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2825", "zh": "在你们的系统里你们直接参与物质实相的形成。你们的自然现像是个人、群众与集体的思想、感觉与情感的具体化。在这方面来说，你的系统比刚才说的那个要较富创造性。在另一方面，在这些其他系统之内，有个强大而革新的“集体意识”正在发展。在其中个人的身份和本体感是保持了，但在个人之间许可有更大的内在活动，有一个大规模的“象征联营”的创造性交流，更方便由其中提取精神上与心灵上的象征。即因如此，这些人更清楚地认知创造性形象与他们对大自然所感知的资料之间的关联。他们故意改变与变化他们对自然所感知的资料，并且拿它来做实验。", "en": "I am not saying that, nor implying it in the case just mentioned. In your system you have a direct hand in the formation of physical reality. Your natural given data is the result of individual, mass, and collective thoughts, feelings, and emotions, materialized. Your system in this respect is more creative than the systems just mentioned. On the other hand, within these other systems there is a strong innovative group consciousness developing, in which identity is retained but greater inner play allowed between individuals, a large creative interchange of symbol-pools, a drawing upon mental and psychic symbols with greater facility. Because of this, these individuals recognize more clearly the connection between creative images and given sense data. They purposely alter and change their given sense data, and experiment with it.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第573节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "573", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "信念怎么变成肉体状况", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e1179", "zh": "听起来或许真的过于简化，不过，你对自己抱持的想法，就会造就出你这个人，你的每个思想确实都会反映在人类组织的实体物质上。这种现象不是来自于什么神秘魔法，也不是装神弄鬼的结果。由于每个人都在潜意识上，创造出符合自己意象的实体物质，因此这种意象的健康状况本来就是他自己要负责。", "en": "It may indeed sound like an oversimplification. However, you are exactly what you think you are, and every thought is mirrored in the physical matter of the human organism. This does not happen by some sort of occult magic. It is not the result of some mumbo jumbo. Since each individual creates subconsciously the physical matter of his own image, then it follows that the condition of this image is his own responsibility.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第162节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "162", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2029", "zh": "如果你想象某些很糟的情境，例如健康不好或孤独绝望，那么这些情境就会自动在现实世界中成真，因为这些想法本身所带来的条件，就会使它们在物质世界中成为实相。如果你想要身体健康，也想要孩子的身体健康，那么就必须尽量以生动逼真的方式想象，就像你常常怀抱着恐惧想象相反的情形一样。", "en": "If you imagine dire circumstances, ill health or desperate loneliness, these will be automatically materialized, for these thoughts themselves bring forth the conditions that will give them reality in physical terms. If you would have good health, if you would have good health for the child, then you must imagine this as vividly as, in fear, you imagine the opposite.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第340节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "340", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2045", "zh": "你知道，这并不意味着这样的理念必定有效，但是在你的系统中，由于它们受到如此强烈的护持，所以肯定会这样子出现。这种强度带来了相应的物质具体化，接着可由感官感知到，而让整个周期变得完整。", "en": "This does not mean that such ideas are necessarily valid, you see, but in your system they certainly appear as such, due to the intensity with which they are held. This intensity brings forth the corresponding physical materiaizationl which the senses then perceive, and the circle becomes complete.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第342节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "342", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "感知不是拍照：你看到的那份物质有你参与造成的部分", "note": "第 23 节先拆掉一个方便的自我形象。你说你几乎以为是某个小小的未知自己在执行呼吸这些必要的功能，事实并非如此；你能接触到自己被你忽略的心智，而这种接触无可避免地会把你带到关于物质世界的真相上——向内工作，你才能更清楚地了解外在。第 265 节留了一个重要的分寸，别让这一段被读成世界是幻觉：他说去看任何一篇讲感官知觉整体本质的科学论文都会发现，感官资料独立于感知者而存在，只是这不一定是从物质的角度来说的。第 289 节说清为什么要转这一道：直接的内在感知你不觉察，物质有机体也感知不到它，因此必须有某些必要的转换，资料可能以视觉或声音的形式出现，而某种解读一向有其必要。\n\n第 803 节把感官本身也交给有意识的单位：你的感官知觉是那些器官的行为的结果，而这些器官在你看来除了与你的关系之外仿佛没有自己的实相；它们本身由有自己意识的原子与分子组成，有自己的感觉与认知状态，它们为你工作，容许你感知物质实相。第 909 节收拢：基本上每个人必须透过直接接触来面对现实的经验，这接触是透过运用肉体感官来感知并诠释物质资讯而发生的，但那些感官的运用本身依赖着你意识的本质。第 3 节给了一个很好用的结论：大多数人没有意识到自己确实有通路达到内在觉知，而你的自我与你的平常意识把你所有的物质经验带入焦点，正是这一步使物质经验那种出色的精确性成为可能。赛斯一边说物质是你创造的，一边把感官这一环当成真实的合作者，而不是当成骗局拆掉——这两件事在他那里不矛盾。", "src": "早期课第1册第 23 节；早期课第6册第 265 节；早期课第7册第 289 节；《个人与群体事件的本质》第 803 节；《梦、进化与价值完成》第 909 节；《健康之道》第 3 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 23 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 265 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 289 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 803 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 909 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 3 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "感官资料有你的一份", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e0102", "zh": "另一件事。你没有有意识地觉察到你的每一次呼吸，在某种程度上是一种方便。但是忽略那个执行呼吸并觉察到呼吸所涉及机制的内我，纯粹是愚蠢透顶的。你在这里几乎以为是某个小小的未知自己在执行着这些必要的功能，事实并非如此。我曾经说过，心智是内在世界的一部分，但是，你能够接触到自己的心智，虽然你忽略它，但是这种接触无可避免地会把你带到物质世界的真相上。向内工作，你便能更加清楚了解外在。", "en": "Another thing. It is in some ways convenient that you are not consciously aware of each breath that you take. But it is sheer stupidity to ignore the inner self which does the breathing, and is aware of the mechanics involved. What you almost get here is that some little unknown self performs these necessary functions, and that is not the case. I have said that the mind is a part of the inner world, but you have access to your own minds which you ignore, and this access would lead you inevitably to the truths about the physical world. Working inward you could understand the outward so much more clearly.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第23节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "23", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e1747", "zh": "研究一下任何以最新感官知觉的整体本质为主题的科学论文，你就会看到感官资料的存在不受感知者左右，但这不一定是从物质的角度来说。", "en": "A study of any up-to-date scientific thesis on the nature of sensual perception in general will show you that sense data exists independent of the perceiver, yet not necessarily in physical terms.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第265节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "265", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e1884", "zh": "你没有觉察到，或鲁柏没有觉察到，直接的内在感知。物质有机体感知它，因此会有一些必要的转变。资料可能以视觉或声音的形式出现。某种解读一向有其必要。", "en": "You are not aware, or Ruburt is not aware, of the direct inner perception. The physical organism cannot perceive it, hence some necessary transformations. The data may make itself known in visual or auditory forms. Some interpretation is always necessary.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第289节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "289", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "但感官这一环也是真的", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e3601", "zh": "就身体而言，你的感官知觉是那些除了与你的关系外，仿佛没有它自己实相的“器官”的行为之结果。那些器官本身是由有它们自己意识的原子与分子组成的。那么它们有自己的感觉与认知状态，它们为你工作，容许你感知物质实相。", "en": "Your sense perception, physically speaking, is a result of behavior on the part of organs that seem to you to have no reality outside of their relationship with you. Those organs are themselves composed of atoms and molecules with their own consciousnesses. They have, then, their own states of sensation and cognition. They work for you, allowing you to perceive physical reality.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第803节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "803", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3818", "zh": "当你出生时，你了解你有一个新的意识，你探索其分支，它是你存在于肉身里的主要证据。基本上，每个人必须透过直接接触来面对现实的经验。当然，这接触是透过运用肉体感官来感知及诠释物质资讯而发生的。不过，那些感官的利用就依赖着你意识的本质，而那意识透过运用自己的属性，来察觉它的力量与行动。", "en": "When you are born, you understand that you have a new consciousness. You explore its ramifications. It is your primary evidence that you exist in flesh. Basically, each person must confront the experience of reality through a direct encounter with it. This encounter takes place through the use of the physical senses, of course, as they are used to perceive and interpret physical data. The very utilization of those senses, however, is dependent upon the nature of your consciousness itself, and that consciousness is aware of its power and action through the exercise of its own properties.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第909节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "909", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3934", "zh": "大多数人不了解，他们的确有通路可以达到这内在的觉知。这内在自我或内在自己不该被认为比你的凡心（ordinary mind）优越。其实，它不该被认为是某个与你的凡心分开的东西。你的自我与你的平常意识将你所有的物质经验带入焦点，而使物质经验之出色的精确性成为可能。", "en": "Most people do not realize that they can indeed have access to this inner awareness. This inner ego or inner self should not be thought of as superior to your ordinary mind. It should not be thought of, really, as something separate from your ordinary mind. Your ego and your ordinary consciousness bring into focus all of your physical experiences, and make possible the brilliant preciseness of physical experience.", "source": "健康之道 · 第3节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "3", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B08", "title": "身体：你一辈子都在重画的那个物质形象", "note": "第 640 节用画家作比，是这一块最好进的入口：一个画家把他的一部分放进画里，你把对自己所知的一切放进身体里，于是身体成为一个具体似的你；对艺术家自己而言画在放下画笔时就完成了，但你在有生之年还在继续创造你的物质形象，并在其中把自己展现出来。第 520 节挪开另一个常见误解：你的身体不是某种把你囚禁其中、像壳子一样存在于你之外的人体模型；你的体型、你切身的个人环境，是你自己的思想、情感与诠释的物质具体化。第 98 节对疾病给的是同一个方向：缺陷并不存在于物质本身，而是被投射于其上。\n\n后面几段说明这件事不只在身体的边界以内。第 162 节说自己也并未受到物质上的限制——那些你认为不属于你自己的化学制品、空气和营养素一直不断地从物质环境进到你自己里面，而那些你认为是属于你自己的东西正从身体的毛细孔离开，所谓边界只是你的感知习惯的结果。第 499 节把这条推到来投胎的存有上：它正把它的原子组合起来、忙着建构必要的装备，而你们两个都在协助它；它把自己知道将会需要的一切知识编织进物质结构里，它已学得的真理将被建造在内。第 867 节给了一个更宽的读法：在微观的层面上并没有像你们这样固定的自我结构，身份是有的，一个细胞并不害怕自己的死亡，它的身份早已在物质实相和无形实相之间来回旅行过太多次。第 672 节把态度变成实际影响：细胞极受你的行为和信念影响，你肯定自己物质存在的正当性，就在无意间仁慈地对待了它们；你不信任自己肉体的天性，细胞与器官也知道，你等于使抗体与你对作。第 709 节替这一段松绑：物质生活本身并不必然需要你们那种自己与肉身的认同。", "src": "早期课第3册第 98 节；早期课第4册第 162 节；早期课第9册第 499 节；《灵魂永生》第 520 节；《个人实相的本质》第 640、672 节；《个人与群体事件的本质》第 867 节；《未知的实相卷二》第 709 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 98 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 162 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 499 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 520 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 640 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 672 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 867 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 709 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "身体是你自己的作品", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e3120", "zh": "一个画家把他的一部分放进画里，你把对自己所知的一切放进你的身体里，因此身体变成了一个具体似的你。一个艺术家爱他的作品。实际上来说，当他放下画笔的时候，那幅画就完成了——至少对他自己而言。那幅画的影响仍在继续。但是在你有生之年，你还在创造你的物质形象，并且把自己展现在其中。", "en": "A painter puts part of himself into a painting. You put all of you of which you are aware into your body, so that it becomes you in flesh. An artist loves his painting. In physical terms it is completed when he puts down his brush — at least for him, though its effects continue. But you are creating your material image as long as you live, and manifesting yourself in it.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第640节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "640", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2607", "zh": "以实质上说，你最初切身的环境就是你的身体。它不是像你被囚禁其中的某种人体解剖模型，存在于你之外像个壳子。你身体的美或丑，健康或残障，敏捷或迟缓，并不是在你出生时就无所选择地强加了给你。相反的，你的体型，你具备的个人环境，是你自己的思想、情感与诠释的物质具体化。", "en": "Now your closest environment, physically speaking, is your body. It is not like some manikin-shape in which you are imprisoned, that exists apart from you like a casing. Your body is not beautiful or ugly, healthy or deformed, swift or slow simply because this is the kind of body that was thrust upon you indiscriminately at birth. Instead your physical form, your corporeal personal environment, is the physical materialization of your own thoughts, emotions, and interpretations.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第520节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "520", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e0762", "zh": "内在的恐惧囊袋（Inner pockets of fear）阻留所需的能量，在身体上创造出这些弱点。透过了解，透过有效率地使用心灵能量，可以发展出效率。缺陷并不存在于物质本身，而是被投射于其上。", "en": "Inner pockets of fear hold back needed energy, creating these weak points in the physical body. Efficiency may be developed through understanding, and through the efficient use of psychic energy. The deficiency is not in the matter itself, but is projected upon it.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第98节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "98", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "边界比你想的软", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e1197", "zh": "你们并没有留住它们，事实上，思想不需要你们意识上的知识，就可以传述，而自己也会扩展。自己也没受到物质上的限制，此外，意念是你们本身感知习惯的结果，因为那些你们认为不属于你们自己的化学制品、空气和营养素，一直不断地从物质环境进到自己里面；而那些你们认为是属于你们自己的东西，却从身体的毛细孔离开。", "en": "You do not hold them. They are indeed transmitted without your conscious knowledge, and the self expands. Nor is the self limited physically. Again, this idea is the result of your own habit of perception, for chemicals and air and nutrients that you consider not your self, enter the self constantly from the physical environment; and that which you consider yourself, leaves through the pores of the body.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第162节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "162", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2507", "zh": "那存有正把它的原子组合起来，忙着建构必要的装备，而你们俩都在协助它。它把它知道自己将需要的一切知识，都编织进物质结构里。可以这么说，它已学得的真理将被建造在内。这个人格所知道的任何东西，都将被写进你们已为它形成的染色体结构里。", "en": "The entity is putting its atoms together, busily constructing the necessary equipment, and you both aid it. It weaves into the physical structure all the knowledge it knows it will need. Truths that it has learned will be built-in, so to speak. Anything that the personality knows will be written into the chromosomal structure that you have formed for it.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第499节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "499", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3694", "zh": "就像你们的想象力在生活中的每个领域都是那么重要，你们的想象力与疾病也是密切相连的。你借由想象性的考虑这样或那样的一个可能性而形成你的存在，而你的思想也以那种方式影响你的身体。以一种方式而言，疾病代表了生命的一种工具，因为人们已经给了疾病社会的、经济的、心理的及宗教的含义，因此它变成了另一个活动与表达的领域。 我告诉过你，在微观的层面并没有像你们自己的那种固定的自我结构。身分的确是有的。一个细胞并不害怕自己的死亡。它的身分已经理所当然的在物质实相和无形实相之间来回旅行太多次了。", "en": "I have told you that at microscopic levels there is no rigid (underlined) self-structure like your own. There is identity. A cell does not fear its own death. Its identity has traveled back and forth from physical to nonphysical reality too often as a matter of course.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第867节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "867", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3164", "zh": "就如动物捡起了它们主人的特性，细胞也极受你的行为和信念影响，如果你肯定你物质存在的“正当性”，那么你就帮助了在你体内的细胞与器官，而在无意间仁慈地对待了它们。如果你不信任你肉体的天性，你也会把这种感觉辐射出来，而不论你采取了哪些保健措施，甚至就像动物一样，细胞与器官也知道你不信任它们。从某方面而言，你使抗体与你作对，只因你不确认肉体存在于时空中的正当性。", "en": "Animals pick up the characteristics of their owners. Cells are highly influenced by your behavior and beliefs. If you affirm the rightness of your physical being, then you help the cells and organs in your body, and without knowing it treat them kindly. If you do not trust your physical nature you radiate this feeling also, regardless of what health procedures you may take. The cells and organs know that you do not trust them, even as animals do. In a way you set up antibodies against yourself, simply because you do not confirm the rightness of your physical being as it exists in space and time.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第672节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "672", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3275", "zh": "我说过，当主要意识与身体分开的时候，身体的确能继续下去，执行必要的维护活动。到某个程度，它甚至能做简单的劳务。（停顿。）事实上，在睡眠里主要意识根本不需要在身体里警醒着。就彼而言，只有在某种的文明里，这样一种身体与主要意识的密切关系才是必要的，因此，有其它的情况，在其中意识常常会游离得远得多，把身体当作一个家以及运作的基地而回来，只为了某种的感知而依赖它，却不依赖它去看到实相的整个画面。物质生活本身并不必然需要你们那种“自己”与肉身的认同。", "en": "I have said (as at 9:48) that the body can indeed carry on, performing necessary maintenance activities while the main consciousness is detached from it. To some extent it can even perform simple chores. (Pause.) In sleep, in fact, it is not at all necessary that the main consciousness be alert in the body. Only in certain kinds of civilizations, for that matter, is such a close body-and-main-consciousness relationship necessary. There are other situations, therefore, in which consciousness ordinarily strays much further, returning to the body as a home station and basis of operation, relying upon it for certain kinds of perception only, but not depending upon it for the entire picture of reality. Physical life alone does not necessarily require the kind of identification of self with flesh that is your own.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第709节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "709", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B09", "title": "要动物质，从还在形成中的那一头动手", "note": "第 75 节给次序：在物质建构得以产生之前，必须先对内在资料或内在结构做心理上的感知、操纵与建构。第 259 节给同一件事的另一面：任何形式首先都是一种潜在于心灵能量之内的形式，因此就你们的物质感知而言，潜在形式早在它的物质显化之前就已经存在。第 625 节把这话推到最具体——他说就某种说法而言，而且是个非常真实的说法，心灵形象是初期的物质；任何由电磁、声与光的值这样组合成的结构，都会自动设法使自己诞生成实质的存在或具体化。第 626 节说出生以前就已经有一次这样的操作：你对将有的身体形成一个精神上的观念，而这个形象被印进物质的方式，是你把自己调整到一个非常明确的实相层面，于是造成一个能在那个密集性区域里活起来、有确实性与有效性的物质结构。第 613 节交代驱动它的那股力：感觉基调是你专为你的实质经验效力的那份能量，它流进身为物质存在的你，把你在这个有四季、空间、血肉和时间的世界里具现出来，而它的根源又相当独立于你所知的世界之外。\n\n第 304 节管住所有走偏的读法：这些知识是帮你利用并指挥物质法则，不是忽略它们；你更有效地运用它们，而且是为了达成内我的目标；你开始创造实体物质好让它确实反映内我，而在这么做的同时，你也造成别人会注意到、并且能当作范例的改变。第 422 节给了同一原理的反面案例：在海滩那件事里，攻击性与破坏性的能量被无意识地向外投射，被给予一个假的实相和暂时的物质有效性，代价是你自己那面的蛋白质损失。第 530 节说任何强烈的精神活动，不管是思想或情感，不仅能以物质性或假物质性的方式来构成事物，还带着构思者相当程度的个性。第 521 节留了一个舞台式的说法：除非多重空间性的我先将自己的一部分物质化，否则无法在三度空间中作戏。", "src": "早期课第2册第 75 节；早期课第6册第 259 节；早期课第7册第 304 节；早期课第9册第 422 节；《个人实相的本质》第 613、625、626 节；《时空之外》第 521、530 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 75 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 259 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 304 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 422 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 613 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 625 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 626 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 521 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 530 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "心灵形象是初期的物质", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e0593", "zh": "只不过，潜意识是在一个非常正当的有效的心理视角之内运作，并能觉察那个视角，而所谓的意识自己对这个心理视角很陌生。在物质建构得以产生之前，必须先进行内在资料或内在结构的心理感知、操纵与建构。", "en": "The subconscious merely is aware of, and operates within, a very valid psychological perspective, with which the so-called conscious self is not familiar. Before physical construction can occur therefore, psychological perception, manipulation and construction of inner data or inner structures must be performed.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第75节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "75", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e1715", "zh": "任何一种形式，而且在梦实相之内也有形式，形式首先全都是一种潜在的形式，存在心灵能量之内。因此，就你们的物质感知而言，潜在形式早在它的物质显化之前就已经存在。", "en": "Form of any kind, and there is form within dream reality, form is first of all a potential form, existing within psychic energy. The potential form therefore exists long before it’s physical materialization, as far as your physical perceptions are concerned.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第259节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "259", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3076", "zh": "当你在心中创造出一个心灵形象时，它也是由刚才所说的同样特质组成的。那么，一个心灵形象也是被某类“光值”（light value）浸染的、具有电磁特性的一个内在声音模式。就某种说法而言，而且是个非常真实的说法，心灵形象是初期的物质（incipient matter）；任何这样组合的结构，结合了电磁、声和光的“值”的结构，就会自动地设法使它自己诞生成实质的存在或具体化。（停了很久。）那么，在这种心灵形象性质与你的身体组合方式上，有一种明确的关系。", "en": "Now: When you create a mental image in your mind it is composed of the same properties just mentioned. A mental image then is also a pattern of internal sound with electromagnetic properties imbued with certain light values. In a sense, and a very real one, the mental image is incipient matter; and any structure so composed, combining the electromagnetic sound and light values, will automatically try to reproduce itself in physical existence, or materialization. (Long pause.) There is a definite connection, then, with the nature of such images and the way in which your body itself is composed.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第625节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "625", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3085", "zh": "那么，在你诞生之前，你对将有的身体形成一个精神上的观念。这个形象以下面这方式“印”到物质里：你把自己调整到一个非常明确的实相层面，造成一个可以生存在那个密集性区域的物质结构，一个有“确实性”与“有效性”的物质结构在那些“频率”里能够活起来的结构（非常肯定地）。", "en": "Before physical birth then you form a mental concept of the body you will have. This image is impressed into matter in this way: You tune yourself into a highly specific dimension of reality. You form a physical structure that will have existence within that intensely concentrated area, that will have validity and actuality — that will come alive within those “frequencies” (very positively).", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第626节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "626", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3041", "zh": "因此，这个“感觉基调”就是你的姿态与气质——音色——专为你的实质经验效力的那份能量。它流进了一个身为物质存在的你，又把你在这个四季运行、有空间、有血肉及时间的世界中具现出来。然而它的根源却又相当独立于你所知的世界之外。", "en": "The feeling-tone then is the motion and fiber — the timber — the portion of your energy devoted to your physical experience. Now it flows into what you are as a physical being and materializes you in the world of seasons, space, flesh, and time. Its source, however, is quite independent of the world that you know.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第613节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "613", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "用它，而不是跟物质法则硬来", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e1927", "zh": "这个知识有助于你利用和指挥物质法则，而不是忽略它们。你更加有效率地利用它们，而且是为了达成内我的目标。你开始创造实体物质，以便它确实反映内我，而且在这么做的同时，你也有其他人注意到并且当作范例的改变。", "en": "This knowledge helps you use and direct physical laws, not ignore them. You use them more efficiently, and for the purposes of the inner self. You begin to create physical matter so that it does indeed reflect the inner self, and in so doing, you effect changes that are noticed by others and serve as an example.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第304节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "304", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2260", "zh": "至于你们的约克海滩形象。在这里，攻击性与破坏性的能量被无意识地向外投射，被给予一个假的实相和暂时的物质有效性。你们自己方面则有蛋白质的损失。", "en": "Now, as to your York Beach images. Here aggressive and destructive energies were unconsciously projected outward, given a pseudo reality and a temporary physical validity. There was a protein loss on your own parts.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第422节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "422", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2957", "zh": "虽然这种思想的形象别人通常都看不见，但是很可能在未来会有科学仪器可以探测得出来；这种形象也能被熟用内在知觉的人感觉得到。任何强烈的精神活动——思想或情感——不仅可以被用来以物质性的或假物质性的方式来构成事物，同时这种精神活动也带有构思者相当程度的个性。", "en": "Though this thought-image usually is not seen by others, it is quite possible that in the future scientific instruments may perceive it. As it is, such an image may be perceived by those who have developed use of the inner senses. Any intense mental act — thought or emotion — will not only be constructed in some physical or pseudophysical manner, but will also bear to some extent the imprint of the personality who originally conceived it.", "source": "时空之外 · 第530节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "530", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2934", "zh": "在这个重要创作的背后，是伟大的协调。每个演员先要使自己在三度空间世界中实际出现，来扮演他所要扮的角色；除非多重空间性的“我”先将自己的一部分物质化，不然就无法在三度空间中作戏。你懂我说的意思吗？", "en": "There is great cooperation behind such momentous productions, and in playing his role, each actor first actualizes himself within three-dimensional reality. The multidimensional self cannot act within three-dimensional reality until it materializes a portion of itself within it. Do you follow me?", "source": "时空之外 · 第521节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "521", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B10", "title": "为什么要有物质世界：它不是惩罚，也不是意外", "note": "赛斯很清楚这套说法很容易把人推成厌世，所以第 538 节把结论直接说出来：灵魂创造肉体是有道理的，创造物质存在也是有道理的，但没有任何理由足以导致你们厌世，也没有任何理由可以让你们对感官的快意或生命中欣悦的事物心如槁木死灰；他说任何向内的探讨都该让你更进一步发现生命的伟大、它的美，以及它对世间生活的意义。第 443 节挡住另一个误读：你们像小孩子在玩一个游戏，却以为人人都在玩这个游戏；物质生命并不是常规，在你们的地球形成之前，本体与意识早就已经存在。第 560 节给了同一件事的数量版本：有许多以物质为主的或然世界，但那只是整个或然系统的一小部分，你们每一位除了存在于物质世界里之外，还同时存在于非物质的世界中。第 571 节说那些人的大部分工作完成于非物质的状态之中，尘世的生涯只不过是有点像去一趟重要的远足。\n\n第 491 节给物质世界一个非常实用的用途。你们系统里的人相对急躁，已经决定跟大量能量打交道，而你们的物理系统本身反应极快，会映出这股能量的运用；作为物理的生物，你们最能对实实在在的物理结果作出回应，所以在任何一股活动浪潮里你们能走多远，非得看到它被客观化方才知晓。他说，倘若你们懂得如何有效地驾驭能量，倘若你们彻底领悟你们的思想才是驱动力、思想本身就是实相，那你们就不需要肉身的存在了——物理环境正是为此而存在的。第 128 节补上另一半：没有在物质宇宙之内体现的心理实相和经验，在电子宇宙之内全部都有它们真实的实相和存在。第 578 节讲谁把这件事意识化了会怎样：他有意识地感知到思想的实相是物质背后的创新者，这样的人在死亡那一刻便能了解种种幻觉的本质，了了分明地进入下一个存在层面，而那些被带到意识层面的情报于是能传给别人，被实际地认知与应用。", "src": "早期课第3册第 128 节；早期课第9册第 443、491 节；《灵魂永生》第 578 节；《时空之外》第 538、560、571 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 128 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 443 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 491 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 578 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 538 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 560 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 571 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "物质生命不是常规，也不是诅咒", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e2972", "zh": "灵魂创造了肉体，但是创造者并不会以高高在上的眼光来看它所创造出来的东西。灵魂创造出肉体有它的道理，创造出物质世界也有它的道理，但是没有任何理由足以导致你们厌世，也没有任何理由可以使得你们对感官的快意或生命中欣悦之事物心如槁木死灰。任何向内的探讨都会让你更进一步发现到生命的伟大、它的美及它对世间生活的意义，若你们全力运用自己之所能，并以欢喜赞叹与精进的态度去探索内心的世界，你们会获得真正满心的愉悦和全面的进展。有了正确的理解之后，你很可能就会变得对死后的一切世界了如指掌，那时你也会发现彼岸的情形“真”得就跟你们的世界一样，这种探索能彻底改变你们以往对死后世界阴森恐怖的观念，你们应该尽量抛却这些错误的观念，这些误谬会阻碍你们的进步。", "en": "The soul creates the flesh. The creator hardly looks down upon its creation. The soul creates the flesh for a reason, and physical existence for a reason, so none of this is to lead you to a distaste for physical life, nor toward a lack of appreciation for those sensual joys with which you are surrounded. Any inner journeys should allow you to find greater significance, beauty, and meaning in life as you know it now; but full enjoyment and development also means that you use all of your abilities, that you explore inner dimensions with as much wonder and enthusiasm. With proper understanding, therefore, it is quite possible for you to become quite familiar now with after-death landscapes and environments and experiences. You will find them to be as vivid as any you know. Such explorations will completely alter somber preconceptions about existence after death. It is very important that you divest yourself of as many preconceptions as possible, however, for these will impede your progress.", "source": "时空之外 · 第538节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "538", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2317", "zh": "按你们的说法，你们就像小孩子在玩一个游戏，而你们以为人人都在玩这个游戏。物质生命并不是常规。在你们的地球形成之前，本体与意识早就已经存在了。", "en": "You are like children, in your terms, with a game, and you think that the game is played by everyone. Physical life is not the rule. Identity and consciousness existed long before your earth was formed.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第443节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "443", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2995", "zh": "有许多的或然世界是以物质为主的，不过这种物质的或然系统只代表了整个或然系统的小小部分。你们每一位除了存在于物质世界里之外，还都同时存在于非物质的世界中。", "en": "There are many probable systems of reality, therefore, in which physical data predominates, but such physical probabilities represent but one small portion. Each of you also exist in nonphysical systems, and I have explained earlier that your slightest thought or emotion is manifested in many other ways than in your own field of existence.", "source": "时空之外 · 第560节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "560", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3010", "zh": "他们大部分的工作完成于非物质的状态之中，尘世的生涯只不过是有点像去一趟重要的远足一样。", "en": "The large amount of their work is done from a nonphysical state, earthly existences being somewhat like very important field trips.", "source": "时空之外 · 第578节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "578", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "它是思想变成实相的那个场所", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e2469", "zh": "你们系统里的人相对急躁，已经决定同大量能量打交道。你们的物理系统本身反应极快，映出这股能量的运用。结果很快就看得见。在群体心灵之中，大聚合与大重排不断发生；种族做出重大决断时，掀起巨大的能量浪潮。这一切都是在无意识的层面上完成的，但作为一种教学方法，结果必须在物质上看到。你们作为物理的生物做出反应，所以你们最能对实实在在的物理结果作出回应。在某一股活动浪潮里，你们能走多远，非得看到它被客观化——或近乎被客观化——方才知晓。倘若你们懂得如何有效地驾驭能量，倘若你们彻底领悟你们的思想才是驱动力、思想本身就是实相，那你们就不需要肉身的存在了——因为物理环境正是为此而存在的。", "en": "Those in your system are relatively impatient, have decided to work with large amounts of energy. Your physical system itself rapidly responds and mirrors the use of this energy. Results are seen quickly. Large groupings and regroupings occur within the mass psyche, huge waves of energy as the race makes important decisions. All of this is done on an unconscious basis, but as a teaching method the results must be seen physically. Because you respond as physical creatures you respond best of all to tangible physical results. You do not know how far you can go in any given waves of activity until you see it objectified, or nearly so. If you knew how to handle energy effectively, if you fully realized that your thoughts were the motivating factor, were the realities, then you would not need a physical existence, for that is the reason for the physical environment.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第491节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "491", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e1002", "zh": "存在这个电子宇宙之内的实相，透过和人类的人格以及其他的互动，而建立起来。没有在物质宇宙之内体现的心理实相和经验，在电子宇宙之内全部都有它们真实的实相和存在。", "en": "Realities existing within this electrical universe are built up through counteractions with the human personality and others. All psychological realities and experiences which are not materialized within the physical universe have their actual reality and existence within the electrical universe.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第128节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "128", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2846", "zh": "他自己那个有意识的肉身取向的部分变得熟识了内在情报。到某个程度，他有意识的感知到“思想的实相”是物质背后的创新者。于是这样一个人在死亡那一刻便能了解种种幻觉的本质，而了了分明的进入下一个存在层面。而那些被带到有意识层面的情报于是便传下去给他人，而能实际地被认知与应用。", "en": "The conscious physically oriented portions of the self become acquainted with the inner information. To some extent the reality of thought is consciously perceived as the innovator behind physical matter. Such an individual then can understand the nature of hallucinations at the point of death, and with full conscious awareness enter into the next plane of existence. The information made conscious is then passed on to others where it can be physically recognized and applied.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第578节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "578", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [{"id": "q-concept-097-e1537", "zh": "在心灵和实际形成你们日常天气、天气循环、季节、干旱，和风暴之间的化学成分中有一个持续的施与受。然后物质天气转而影响每个个人的心灵氛围。引发你们天气的动力可以认为是自己生成的。", "en": "There is a constant give and take between psychic and chemical components which actually cause your daily weather, your weather cycles, seasons, droughts and storms. This physical weather then in its turn affects and changes the psychic atmosphere of each individual. The force that causes your weather can be thought of as self-generating.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第228节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "228", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3146", "zh": "以你们来说，意识是与物质结合的，它的任何经验是借着相互作用而实质具体化。例如，在暴风雨与心灵风暴之间有很大的相关性，而在情感与思想两者不稳的电磁特性、大脑处理它们的能力，以及大脑排除多余东西的需要之间，也有很大的相关性。你不只是对天气反应，而且是你协助来形成它——甚至当你吸进空气而后再吐出时。大脑是你所不了解的一个电磁关系之“巢”。以某种说法，大脑是个控制下的风暴。", "en": "In your terms consciousness is wedded with matter, and any of its experiences are physically materialized through that interaction. There are great correlations between thunderstorms and psychic storms, for example, and between unstable electromagnetic properties of both feeling and thought, the brain’s ability to handle these, and its need to rid itself of excesses. You do not simply react to the weather. You help form it, even as you breathe the air and then send it outward again. The brain is a nest of electromagnetic relationships that you do not understand. In certain terms it is a controlled storm.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第664节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "664", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3929", "zh": "你不会“伤”一个旱灾。你也不会伤风。以一种说法，一个旱灾是部分地被经验它的那些人引起的——然而，一个旱灾并非一个疾病。它是一个过程的一部分。它是世界物质上的稳定性之更大过程的一个必要部分。虽然一个旱灾可能看来很不幸，以其自己的方式，它是为整个行星表面、湿度平衡的比例负责的。同样的，疾病以它们的方式也往往是更大过程的一部分，其更大目的是身体的整体平衡与（停顿良久）力量。", "en": "(Long pause at 4:25.) You do not “catch” a drought. You do not catch a cold, either. In a fashion a drought is partially caused by the emotional states of the people who experience it — yet a drought is not a disease. It is part of a process. It is a necessary portion of the larger process of the world’s physical stability. As unfortunate as a drought might seem, it is in its way responsible for the balanced proportion of moisture of the entire planet’s surface. In the same way diseases in their fashion are also often parts of larger processes whose greater purpose is the body’s overall balance and (long pause) strength.", "source": "健康之道 · 第2节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "2", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3625", "zh": "万物都是能量的一个表现——能量的一个情感性显现。人能以气压与气流的方式诠释天气，他看断层线来了解地震，在某一个层面，到某一个程度，所有这些均是有用的。可是，人的心灵在情感上不只是他物理环境的一部分，也与所有大自然化现的现象密切相连。用一下在上一章开始谈到的那些用语，那我会说，人在情感上与自然的认同在“架构二”里是一个被强烈感受到的实相。而我们必须在那儿寻找关于人与自然关系的答案。在“架构二”里，心灵的本质十分清楚的显现，因此，其范围与节奏能被了解。物质能量之显现追随着情感上的节奏，那是不论多精密的精巧玩意儿或仪器所无法确定的。", "en": "All being is manifestation of energy — an emotional manifestation of energy. Man can interpret the weather in terms of air pressure and wind currents. He can look to fault lines in an effort to understand earthquakes. All of this works at a certain level, to a certain degree. Man’s psyche, however, is emotionally not only a part of his physical environment, but intimately connected with all of nature’s manifestations. Using the terms begun in the last chapter, I will say then that man’s emotional identification with nature is a strongly-felt reality in Framework 2. And there we must look for the answers regarding man’s relationship with nature. There in Framework 2 the nature of the psyche appears quite clearly, so that its sweeps and rhythms can be understood. The manifestations of physical energy follow emotional rhythms that cannot be ascertained with gadgets or instruments, however fine.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第817节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "817", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3243", "zh": "以感官上来说，他会对那个橘子学得很少，虽然他也许能分离其成分，预言其他的橘子在那儿可以被找到，对它的环境有一番理论——但那橘子更大的“内里”也无法在它皮内的任何地方被找到。种子是未来橘子的物质性携带者，但形成那些种子的却是橘子未来实相的蓝图。在这种困境里，你永远被带回到那一个先来的问题里，而开始一个狗追尾巴的游戏，因为你们以连续性时间的方式来思想，好像看起来就必须有第一个蛋或种子似的，不过，实相的蓝图却存在于没有这样一个时间顺序的次元里。", "en": "In sense terms he would learn little about an orange, though he might be able to isolate its elements, predict where others might be found, theorize about its environment — but the greater “withinness” of the orange is not found any place inside of its skin either. The seeds are the physical carriers of future oranges, but the blueprints for that reality are what formed the seeds. In such dilemmas you are always brought back to the question of which came first, and begin another merry chase. Because you think in terms of consecutive time, it seems that there must have been a first egg, or seed.1 The blueprints for reality exist, however, in dimensions without such a time sequence. Your closest point to the withinness of which I speak is your own consciousness, though you use it as a tool to examine the exterior universe. But it is basically free of that reality, not confined to the life-and-death saga, and at other levels deals with the blueprints for its own physical existence.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第703节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "703", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3002", "zh": "上面所举的只是一些小小的例子，在某种程度上说明了一些你意识所具有的机动性，以及你是如何收放自如的在运用这种机动性而已。很奇特的，“象征”往往可以被当作是某种“样品”，以显示你在不同的意识层次中所感知的事情，而“象征”所显示出的各种变化，则可以被用作各种情况的“指标”。比如说，“火”就是由某种“象征”转化而成的景象；在实际世界中的“火”，是你用物质世间的意识所感知的“现实”；而一幅在心像中的火景，则自动说明了意识所涉及的是其他的层面。", "en": "To some extent, all of these are small examples of the mobility of your consciousness, and the ease with which it can be used. In a strange manner, symbols can be regarded as samples of the way you perceive at various levels of consciousness. Their changing guises can be used as signposts. Fire, for example, is a symbol made physical, so a real fire tells you obviously that you are perceiving reality with your physically attuned consciousness.", "source": "时空之外 · 第571节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "571", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3254", "zh": "“在这些边袋里，所谓的记忆并不是这样结构的，其始终存在的活生生成分，以及其生长是很明显的。其资料一直是新鲜的。在此，过去仍然在发生。我们通常透过神经联系而经验到它，在那时它看来就仿佛是栩栩如生或活泼泼的，但其实它一直都是如此。过去的动作与行为仍在继续，而非重新发生——这很难解释——但那些过去的行动仍在探索其他的可能性，同时，我们的神经结构使我们聚焦在我们选择的这一个（物质的）可能实相里。对我们而言，那些其他的行动似乎中止了……但那只因为我们通常无法跟随它们。”", "en": "“In these side pockets, memory, so-called, is not so structured. Its ever-present living elements are apparent; and its growth. Its material is ever-fresh. Here the past still happens. Usually we experience it through neurological connections; that’s when it seems vivid or alive, but actually it’s that way all the time. Past motion and acts still go on, not recurring — it’s hard to explain — but those past actions are still exploring other probabilities, while our nervous structure focuses us in the one (physical) probable reality we’ve chosen. To us those other actions seem terminated … but that’s only because usually we can’t follow them.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第704节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "704", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3467", "zh": "由于你是有血有肉的生物，感知的内在层面就必须有它们在实质上的对等物，但要不是有这些内在的网络，根本就不可能有物质的觉察和身体上的反应……我是说，所有外在事件，包括你自己的身体从里到外，所有的物体，所有的具体显现，全都是“内在结构”的对等“外在结构”，而内在结构则全是由声音及看不见的光所组合而交织成的电磁模式。", "en": "Because you are flesh and blood creatures, the interior aspects of perception must have their physical counterparts. But material awareness and bodily response to it would be impossible were it not for these internal webworks … I am saying that all exterior events, including your own bodies with their insides, all objects, all physical materializations, are the outside structures of inside ones that are composed of interior sound and invisible light, interwoven in electromagnetic patterns.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第744节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "744", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e1651", "zh": "我想强调在我们上一节提到的一些重点，特别是你只感知任何既定行动的一小部分，即使那个行动的某些起源是在你自己的物质场域之内。", "en": "I want to stress some points mentioned in our last session, to the effect in particular that you perceive only a small portion of any given action even when that action has some of its origins within your own physical field.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第249节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "249", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e1795", "zh": "当自我经由训练而更能觉察到这个内我时，整个人格都会受益。透过研究物质导向的自我在物质操纵当中可见的行动，以及研究梦经验当中可见的内在自我的活动，就可以一瞥存在任何既定时间的全我。显然，在实现这个目标之前，必须进行一些训练。", "en": "When through training the ego becomes more aware of this inner self, the whole personality benefits. The whole self as it exists at any given time can be glimpsed through studying the actions of the physically-oriented ego, as seen in physical manipulation, and in studying the activities of the inner ego as seen in dream experiences. Obviously some training is necessary before this can be achieved.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第273节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "273", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e2450", "zh": "去解决你们的问题、胜过你们的挑战……而推动力是这样的：在你们觉得自己在物质实相里安顿下来之前，不可进入内在的实相……因为除非你们在一个世界里是安稳的，你们就无法同时活在两个世界里。你们需要一块坚实的地基……一块你们能够信任的地基。那时你们才能走过其他那些门，但你们必须能在这个宇宙里两脚站稳。……而那时你们就会自觉地走到你们的身体不能跟随的地方……你们就会找到你们的答案。但你们必须有一样安稳的东西可以攀住。再没有比这更好的理由，去解决你们的问题了。", "en": "... to solve your problems and triumph over your challenges.... and the impetus is this: you must not journey into inner reality until you feel secure in physical reality.... for you cannot live in two worlds at once unless you are secure in one. You need a firm groundwork... a groundwork that you can trust. And then you can travel through these other doors, but you must be able to stand on your two feet in this universe.... And then you will go consciously where your body cannot follow... and you will find your answers. But you must have something secure to hang onto. Now there is no better reason to solve your problems.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第485节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "485", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-097-e3183", "zh": "很不幸的，我们必须常用比喻，因为它们能在观念之间形成桥梁。那么，就如那儿有物质的单位一样，那儿也有意识的单位。我不要你们把这些单位想作是粒子。有一个意识的基本单位，它一旦被表达出来就不会再被分裂得更小了，就如以前人们以为一个原子是最小的单位，而不能被分得更小一样。这意识的基本单位显然不是具体的，它在它自己内天生的包含着扩张、发展及组织等的无限特性；然而，在它自己内永远维持着它自己的个别性之核心。不论它变成什么组织的一部分或它与其他此种基本单位如何混合，它自己的身份不会被消灭。", "en": "We must unfortunately often deal with analogies, because they can form bridgeworks between concepts. There are units of consciousness,3 then, as there are units of matter. I do not want you to think of these units as particles. There is a basic unit of consciousness that, expressed, will not be broken down, as once it was thought that an atom was the smallest unit and could not be broken down. The basic unit of consciousness obviously is not physical. It contains within itself innately infinite properties of expansion, development, and organization; yet within itself always maintains the kernel of its own individuality. Despite whatever organizations it becomes part of, or how it mixes with other such basic units, its own identity is not annihilated.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第682节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "682", "only_en": false}], "books": [{"name": "早期课第2册", "count": 11}, {"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 7}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 6}, {"name": "个人实相的本质", "count": 6}, {"name": "时空之外", "count": 6}, {"name": "个人与群体事件的本质", "count": 5}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 5}, {"name": "心灵的本质", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 5}, {"name": "未知的实相卷二", "count": 4}, {"name": "未知的实相卷一", "count": 4}, {"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 4}, {"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 4}, {"name": "健康之道", "count": 3}, {"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 3}, {"name": "早期课第8册", "count": 3}, {"name": "早期课第5册", "count": 1}], "span": [1963, 1984], "stats": {"blocks": 10, "quotes": 89, "reading": 12, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 0, "only_en": 3}};
